.TH AVR\-SERVICE\-TOKEN 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-service-token \- Create and manage the organization's service tokens.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr service-token
[OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create and manage the organization's service tokens.
.PP
A service token (avt_...) belongs to a group of one organization rather than to a person, and keeps working when its creator leaves. It reads only the repositories and egress firewall rules its access names. Organization admins manage service tokens while signed in with `avr auth login`; a scoped or service token cannot. To use a service token, set AVR_TOKEN to its secret.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
create
Create a service token and print its secret once.
.TP
list
List the organization's service tokens, soonest expiry first.
.TP
revoke
Revoke a service token.
.TP
revoke-all
Revoke every service token of the organization.
.TP
rotate
Issue a service token a new secret and print it once.
.TP
set-access
Replace a service token's whole access selection.
.TP
view
Show a service token's details, versions and grants.
